    <h2>Separate the session from the transport. Then make it hard to kill.</h2>
    <div class="how">
      <div><span class="k">01 · HYBRID CARRIER</span><h3>QUIC and TLS WebSocket, raced on every connect</h3><p>QUIC gets a 300 ms head start; if UDP is blocked, the WebSocket wins. Nothing to configure.</p></div>
      <div><span class="k">02 · HOLDER</span><h3>Connections come and go. The session stays.</h3><p>One process per session on the host keeps the PTY, the screen and your unacked input.</p></div>
      <div><span class="k">03 · FLIGHT CONTROL</span><h3>A download can't bury your echo</h3><p>Keystrokes go ahead of bulk, and a slow link gets the latest screen, not a backlog.</p></div>
    </div>
